386
00:17:44.577 --> 00:17:45.943
Here is a quick table:

387
00:17:46.223 --> 00:17:47.951
Fix, and How, and Trade-off.

388
00:17:48.231 --> 00:17:49.767
Versioned conditional set.

389
00:17:50.047 --> 00:17:50.708
How:

390
00:17:50.988 --> 00:18:00.823
Store version, value and only SET if the incoming version ≥ the cached version (Lua); the delete writes a tombstone with the new version.

391
00:18:01.103 --> 00:18:01.999
Trade-off:

392
00:18:02.279 --> 00:18:07.377
Needs a monotonic version from the SoR (row version column); a small Lua script.

393
00:18:07.657 --> 00:18:08.809
Short TTL.

394
00:18:09.089 --> 00:18:09.751
How:

395
00:18:10.031 --> 00:18:11.567
Bounds the staleness window.

396
00:18:11.847 --> 00:18:12.743
Trade-off:

397
00:18:13.023 --> 00:18:14.601
Only reduces the damage.

398
00:18:14.881 --> 00:18:16.247
Delayed double delete.

399
00:18:16.527 --> 00:18:17.188
How:

400
00:18:17.468 --> 00:18:20.241
Delete, then delete again after ~1 s.

401
00:18:20.521 --> 00:18:21.417
Trade-off:

402
00:18:21.697 --> 00:18:23.639
Heuristic; timing-dependent.

403
00:18:23.919 --> 00:18:26.052
Lease tokens (Facebook memcache).

404
00:18:26.332 --> 00:18:26.993
How:

405
00:18:27.273 --> 00:18:33.524
A miss returns a lease; the set is accepted only with a valid lease, and a delete invalidates leases.

406
00:18:33.804 --> 00:18:34.700
Trade-off:

407
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.260
Needs cache support.

408
00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:40.767
Update the cache from the change stream only (CDC).

409
00:18:41.047 --> 00:18:41.709
How:

410
00:18:41.989 --> 00:18:45.573
Only the CDC consumer writes the cache, in commit order.

411
00:18:45.853 --> 00:18:46.749
Trade-off:

412
00:18:47.029 --> 00:18:49.909
More infrastructure; the app never writes the cache.

413
00:18:51.259 --> 00:18:58.149
L3 implements versioned conditional sets with version tombstones, which is simple and robust with Redis Lua.

414
00:18:59.499 --> 00:19:01.270
Invalidation across layers.

415
00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:06.627
There are only two hard things in Computer Science: cache invalidation and naming things.

416
00:19:06.907 --> 00:19:07.974
Phil Karlton.

417
00:19:09.324 --> 00:19:10.689
