00:25:06.405 --> 00:25:07.151
Note:

532
00:25:07.431 --> 00:25:10.205
What the system guarantees after this failure path.

533
00:25:10.485 --> 00:25:26.101
A stale value can never overwrite a newer one, and a delete can't be undone by a slow reader, because every write to L2 carries the SoR version and the Lua script accepts only versions ≥ the stored one (including tombstones).

534
00:25:26.381 --> 00:25:28.855
The worst case is a transient extra miss.

535
00:25:29.135 --> 00:25:34.319
L1 staleness is bounded by its 5 s TTL even if a broadcast is missed.

536
00:25:34.599 --> 00:25:37.159
Checkout always re-prices from the SoR.

537
00:25:38.509 --> 00:25:41.475
State: a cache entry with soft and hard TTLs.

