628
00:31:15.251 --> 00:31:35.773
TTL 6h ± 10%. key: v1:price:store:sku value: v:9,d:paise:100 TTL 10m ± 10%. tomb: v1:price:store:sku value: v:10,t:1 TTL 60s (only blocks older writes). hot: v1:card:sku0..

629
00:31:36.053 --> 00:31:39.957
7 replicas for the top-500 SKUs during sales.

630
00:31:42.807 --> 00:31:53.858
The v1: prefix is the cache schema version: changing the payload format means bumping it to v2:, with no flush and no deserialization errors during a rolling deploy.

