00:39:45.650 --> 00:39:55.101
L2 entries are Redis HASHes: v (SoR version), d (payload) t=1 (tombstone), e (soft expiry ms), c (compute ms).

770
00:39:55.381 --> 00:40:01.290
Writes go through SETIFNEWER, so an older version can never overwrite a newer value or tombstone.

771
00:40:01.570 --> 00:40:03.277
KEYS1=key ARGV:

772
00:40:03.557 --> 00:40:15.482
1=version 2=payload 3=ttlMs 4=isTombstone(0 or 1) 5=softExpiryMs 6=computeMs.

773
00:40:18.332 --> 00:40:22.599
Two-level cache (Caffeine + Redis + XFetch + DB guard).

774
00:40:22.879 --> 00:40:24.415
