808
00:43:12.120 --> 00:43:14.339
(Same pattern as Ch 01.).

809
00:43:17.189 --> 00:43:17.935
Warning:

810
00:43:18.215 --> 00:43:20.967
Order of L1 and L2 invalidation.

811
00:43:21.247 --> 00:43:31.551
If a pod evicts L1 before the invalidator has written the L2 tombstone, the next L1 miss can re-read the old L2 value and cache it for up to 5 s.

812
00:43:31.831 --> 00:43:35.095
That's acceptable here (it's the L1 TTL bound).

813
00:43:35.375 --> 00:43:44.058
To tighten it, have the invalidator publish a secondary cache.invalidated event after writing L2, and drive L1 eviction from that.

814
00:43:45.408 --> 00:43:46.347
