817
00:43:52.520 --> 00:43:59.475
Hot keys (sale SKUs) get N replicas with different names, then different hash slots, then different Redis shards.

818
00:43:59.755 --> 00:44:04.213
Reads pick a random replica; invalidations tombstone all replicas.

819
00:44:07.063 --> 00:44:17.751
The two-level cache uses hotKeys.readKey(key) for L2 reads and writes all replicas on a fill (each with setIfNewer, so replicas can't go backwards either).

820
00:44:18.031 --> 00:44:28.485
With L1 in front, each pod reads a hot key from Redis at most about once per 5 s, so replication matters most when L1 is cold (deploys, scale-out).

